+}
+
+/// The body's own exponent `k` for its fictitious step `ds_unit·2^-k`, from a dimensionless coupling
+/// κ = `u`/`c` the caller bounds by the body's own orbit (step.rs `coupling_bound`): one bit of Δs per octave
+/// of κ — Sundman's slope — anchored where κ = 1 at `k_max` (for one source, the doll's edge scale R_H/r), and
+/// floored `RAMP_LOG2` octaves below (the bulk: 16 kicks per P_D at the shipped 7). `k_max` for every κ at
+/// once is the shipped doll-wide constant. Because κ is a property of the orbit, not of the position, the
+/// sequence of steps changes only when the orbit does — a librating moon holds one cadence through every
+/// conjunction (a position-based κ chatters at the synodic frequency and breaks the split's time symmetry).
+pub fn split_k(k_max: i32, u: Scalar, c: Scalar) -> i32 {
+    let bulk = k_max - RAMP_LOG2;
+    if !u.is_positive() {
+        return bulk;
+    }
+    // ceil(log2 κ) = −floor(log2 c/κ), exact on the grid; κ ≥ 1 (an orbit that will encounter) clamps to the anchor.
+    match c.div(u) {
